U-Boot loader and related files for the Banana Pi BPI-R64 (MediaTek MT7622)

The bootloader boots from the SD card.  BL2 and BL31 come from MediaTek's
Trusted Firmware-A fork, U-Boot finds the operating system through
standard boot (EFI/BOOT/bootaa64.efi on the EFI system partition).

  bl2.img     BL2 for the SD card (2x DDR3)
  fip.bin     FIP with BL31 and U-Boot
  sdcard.img  First 6 MiB of a bootable SD card: GPT with a hybrid MBR
              and the bl2, fip and ubootenv partitions

The MT7622 BootROM finds BL2 through the MBR and BL2 finds the FIP through
the GPT partition named "fip", so the card has to keep this layout.

To install the bootloader on an sdcard (da0) and add partitions for
FreeBSD after the first 6 MiB:

dd if=/usr/local/share/u-boot/u-boot-bananapi-r64/sdcard.img of=/dev/da0 bs=1m
gpart recover da0
gpart add -t efi -b 6m -s 64m da0
gpart add -t freebsd-ufs da0
dd if=/usr/local/share/u-boot/u-boot-bananapi-r64/sdcard.img of=/dev/da0 bs=512 count=1

gpart replaces the hybrid MBR with a plain protective MBR, the last dd
puts it back.  Run it again after any later gpart change on the card.

To update U-Boot on a card that already has this layout:

dd if=/usr/local/share/u-boot/u-boot-bananapi-r64/fip.bin of=/dev/da0p2 bs=1m conv=sync
